            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Create_Draft_Email</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Drafted</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Parallel AI drafting for Origin=Email Cases. Runs independently of the (external) triage/assignment system and does NOT touch triage-owned fields: it classifies intake first (CaseIntakeClassifier: junk mail is stamped NO_DRAFT_EXCLUDED with zero callouts, billing/licensing threads go to the orchestrator pre-excluded), then reads the Case (Subject/Description/Product_List__c), generates a grounded reply via SupportDraftOrchestrator, and stamps ONLY the AI_Draft_* fields. On a DRAFTED outcome it also creates a Draft-status EmailMessage (CaseDraftEmailPublisher) so an agent can review/edit/send it from the Case Feed -- requires "Enable Email Drafts" in Support Settings. An escalate-only top match posts a Slack alert. Never sends to the customer; the draft is left on the Case for a human to review.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>IsBillingExcluded</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>{!Classify_Intake.category} = &quot;BILLING&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
